WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:16.462
froze with fear.

2
00:00:16.982 --> 00:00:21.365
She had two choices: she could pretend she didn't hear whoever was behind her and walk away.

3
00:00:21.886 --> 00:00:23.987
Or, choice two, she could run away!

4
00:00:24.588 --> 00:00:27.810
But before she could do anything at all, the person stepped in front of her.

5
00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:30.652
Mateo's eyes were wide, and his jaw hung open.

6
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.162
"Did what I think just happened really just happen?

7
00:00:34.702 --> 00:00:41.687
That was Are you a "Please, Mateo, don't tell anyone what you saw," Ally pleaded.

8
00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:43.529
"My ship broke down.

9
00:00:43.989 --> 00:00:47.211
I need parts and fuel, and once I get them, I'm going to leave.

10
00:00:47.551 --> 00:00:48.912
I came to Earth in peace!"

11
00:00:50.053 --> 00:00:51.634
"I knew it," he murmured.

12
00:00:52.515 --> 00:00:56.518
"When I saw you onstage before "Please don't tell anyone!"

13
00:00:56.918 --> 00:00:57.598
Ally repeated.

14
00:00:57.618 --> 00:00:59.420
"It could put me in danger!"

15
00:01:07.504 --> 00:01:08.925
"I won't," Mateo said.

16
00:01:08.945 --> 00:01:11.066
"But I do have to say one thing."

17
00:01:12.687 --> 00:01:13.368
Ally gulped.

18
00:01:13.388 --> 00:01:17.230
"You were robbed!"

19
00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:17.970
he said.

20
00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:21.172
"Someone stole my pod?"

21
00:01:21.192 --> 00:01:24.634
"No." Mateo smiled.

22
00:01:24.654 --> 00:01:28.557
"You totally should have won first prize in the contest!"

23
00:01:29.897 --> 00:01:30.978
Ally laughed with relief.

24
00:01:30.998 --> 00:01:33.540
"Oh! I agree.

25
00:01:36.424 --> 00:01:38.965
So you're not mad at me for lying to you?"

26
00:01:38.985 --> 00:01:42.326
"No way," Mateo said.

27
00:01:42.346 --> 00:01:46.027
"I mean, how many people can say their good friend is an alien?"

28
00:01:47.447 --> 00:01:49.468
Touched, Ally put a hand on her heart.

29
00:01:49.488 --> 00:01:52.129
"You think of me as your good friend?"

30
00:01:52.149 --> 00:01:57.490
"We haven't known each other long, but you've been really helpful to Papi and me."

31
00:01:58.571 --> 00:02:00.111
Ally's eyes filled with tears.

32
00:02:00.791 --> 00:02:02.652
An Earthling was calling her a good friend!

33
00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:07.962
Her parents would be thrilled at all the peaceful cooperation she'd achieved on this planet.

34
00:02:19.827 --> 00:02:21.527
make you a deal," Mateo said.

35
00:02:21.547 --> 00:02:25.489
"Since I know your big secret, I'll tell you mine."

36
00:02:25.509 --> 00:02:28.930
"You don't have to do that," Ally said.

37
00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:32.392
"I want to," Mateo replied.

38
00:02:34.624 --> 00:02:36.566
"I've never told this to anyone.

39
00:02:38.067 --> 00:02:39.448
I know where my mom is.

40
00:02:40.309 --> 00:02:41.290
She texts me.

41
00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:44.633
She's trying to pursue a new career and live on her own.

42
00:02:45.813 --> 00:02:49.877
But she's worried if my dad knows, he'll try to convince her to come back home."

43
00:02:49.897 --> 00:02:54.261
"Wow, that's a huge secret," Ally said.

44
00:02:54.281 --> 00:02:56.683
"Thank you for trusting me with it."

45
00:02:56.703 --> 00:03:02.107
"Well, it's not quite as big as being an alien," Mateo said.

46
00:03:04.736 --> 00:03:06.517
"So where are these parts you need?"

47
00:03:08.759 --> 00:03:10.320
Ally got teary-eyed again.

48
00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:14.503
"I thought they were here in Sandville, but it turns out Dr.

49
00:03:14.543 --> 00:03:15.824
Lloyd lured my ship here.

50
00:03:15.884 --> 00:03:20.087
So She swallowed hard.

51
00:03:20.107 --> 00:03:22.889
"I don't know if I'll ever get home."

52
00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:26.531
Mateo put an arm around her shoulder.

53
00:03:26.551 --> 00:03:28.213
"I'll help you figure it out.

54
00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:32.836
For now, why don't we find the others and head back to the diner."

55
00:03:35.996 --> 00:03:39.959
As Ally and Mateo headed to the main hall, she told him all about Dr.

56
00:03:39.979 --> 00:03:40.920
Lloyd's discoveries.

57
00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.883
"His research has lots of inaccuracies," she said.

58
00:03:44.903 --> 00:03:47.765
"But he's not totally misinformed.

59
00:03:48.846 --> 00:03:54.130
And if he finds out about me, I bet he'll She swallowed hard again.

60
00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:57.012
"Try to use me for more research!"

61
00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:06.750
At the diner Barry was wiping down tables, and Flo and Ray were chatting behind the counter.

62
00:04:10.873 --> 00:04:13.474
kids!" Ray greeted them with a big smile.

63
00:04:13.494 --> 00:04:15.235
"How was the convention?"

64
00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:19.778
"Interesting." Mateo traded glances with Ally.

65
00:04:19.798 --> 00:04:22.719
"How about some ice cream on the house?"

66
00:04:23.159 --> 00:04:23.640
Ray said.

67
00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:26.401
"Yes!" everyone said.

68
00:04:26.421 --> 00:04:30.103
"He's in a good mood," Mateo whispered to Ally.

69
00:04:30.584 --> 00:04:31.164
Ally nodded.

70
00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:37.425
Ray did seem happy, and she knew why: Ray's and Flo's thoughts were suddenly coming to her loud

71
00:04:37.465 --> 00:04:37.865
and clear.

72
00:04:38.666 --> 00:04:41.488
They were both thinking about how much they enjoyed each other's company.

73
00:04:41.508 --> 00:04:45.751
"I did make Ray happy," Ally thought.

74
00:04:45.771 --> 00:04:47.953
"I did it by hiring Flo!"

75
00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:50.996
It was another good deed that would impress her parents.

76
00:04:54.418 --> 00:04:57.381
Ally was about to dig into her bowl of ice cream when Barry came over.

77
00:04:57.401 --> 00:05:00.964
"When are you going to teach me that levitating trick?"

78
00:05:02.144 --> 00:05:04.885
"Why is he so desperate to learn that?"

79
00:05:05.365 --> 00:05:06.385
Ally thought, annoyed.

80
00:05:07.165 --> 00:05:10.526
She did a quick scan of his thoughts, but all she could see was an image of a

81
00:05:10.566 --> 00:05:12.667
man, likely his father, looking proud.

82
00:05:14.387 --> 00:05:15.508
She felt her heart soften.

83
00:05:15.528 --> 00:05:18.348
"I understand that feeling," she thought.

84
00:05:18.368 --> 00:05:21.209
"I want my parents to be proud of me too."

85
00:05:21.229 --> 00:05:23.270
"Soon, Barry."

86
00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:28.091
Ally held crossed fingers behind her back, the way humans did when telling white lies.

87
00:05:28.851 --> 00:05:31.112
For once Barry took that for an answer and walked away.

88
00:05:32.296 --> 00:05:34.298
Ally kept her fingers crossed for another minute.

89
00:05:35.019 --> 00:05:37.342
But it wasn't because she was about to tell another lie.

90
00:05:37.922 --> 00:05:42.287
It was because humans often crossed their fingers for another reason—luck.

91
00:05:43.608 --> 00:05:46.732
With Mateo's help, maybe she could figure out a way to get home soon.
